IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `asic-consumer`

-- Australian Securities and Investments Commission Act 2001 (Cth), Part 2 (ss 11, 12A; Division 2) and Part 3 ss 13, 19, 23, 30,
-- 63, 68 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked against a
-- decided case. No regulations are deposited; the s 12BC "greater amount" and the penalty unit value are inputs.
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_australian-securities-and-investments-commission-act-2001_baseline.py). Expected results
-- were written by hand from the text.

-- Facts from the WA lives (workbench scenarios au/wa/cradle-to-grave-*): Jarrah Legal Technologies Pty Ltd is registered with
-- ASIC on 15 March 2031, 70% Daniel's, 10% Priya's, 20% a sophisticated investor's for $500,000, with an ABN and a business
-- name; three employees from June (d043). Jake takes two credit cards at 24 on 2 March 2031 (k048) and on 6 February 2037 owes
-- $41,000 and collectors call (k064); the Competition and Consumer Act baseline found that credit card debt collection falls
-- under this Act's s 12DJ. The lives give no pitch to the investor, no bank contract, no account of what the collectors did and
-- no ASIC inquiry: those facts are ASSUMED, and each judgment the Act leaves to a court (misleading, unconscionable, unfair,
-- undue harassment) is set by hand. The penalty unit value used (330) is an ASSUMED input, not read from any deposit.

`d043: Jarrah issuing its shares to the investor` MEANS `What the other side does` WITH
    `the thing supplied is itself a financial product` IS FALSE
    `gives financial product advice` IS FALSE
    `applies for, acquires, issues, varies or disposes of a financial product` IS TRUE
    `does so only on its own behalf` IS TRUE
    `is the issuer of the product dealt in` IS TRUE
    `does another thing listed in s 12BAB(1)(c)-(h)` IS FALSE

`k048: the bank supplying Jake a credit card` MEANS `What the other side does` WITH
    `the thing supplied is itself a financial product` IS TRUE
    `gives financial product advice` IS FALSE
    `applies for, acquires, issues, varies or disposes of a financial product` IS FALSE
    `does so only on its own behalf` IS FALSE
    `is the issuer of the product dealt in` IS FALSE
    `does another thing listed in s 12BAB(1)(c)-(h)` IS FALSE

`k064: Jake's credit card, a household kind of service` MEANS `My acquisition of financial services` WITH
    `price` IS 41000
    `a greater prescribed amount` IS 0
    `of a kind ordinarily acquired for personal, domestic or household use or consumption` IS TRUE
    `acquired for use in connection with my small business` IS FALSE
    `of a kind ordinarily acquired for business use or consumption` IS FALSE

`a 60000 business loan service, not of a business kind` MEANS `My acquisition of financial services` WITH
    `price` IS 60000
    `a greater prescribed amount` IS 0
    `of a kind ordinarily acquired for personal, domestic or household use or consumption` IS FALSE
    `acquired for use in connection with my small business` IS FALSE
    `of a kind ordinarily acquired for business use or consumption` IS FALSE

`Jarrah's 60000 business account, of a business kind` MEANS `My acquisition of financial services` WITH
    `price` IS 60000
    `a greater prescribed amount` IS 0
    `of a kind ordinarily acquired for personal, domestic or household use or consumption` IS FALSE
    `acquired for use in connection with my small business` IS TRUE
    `of a kind ordinarily acquired for business use or consumption` IS TRUE

`a bank term letting it vary the fees at will` MEANS `The term` WITH
    `causes a significant imbalance in rights and obligations` IS TRUE
    `the advantaged party proved it reasonably necessary to protect its legitimate interests` IS FALSE
    `would cause me detriment if applied or relied on` IS TRUE
    `defines the main subject matter of the contract` IS FALSE
    `sets the upfront price` IS FALSE
    `is required or expressly permitted by a law` IS FALSE
    `is a transparent insurance excess disclosed before the contract` IS FALSE

`the same term, shown reasonably necessary` MEANS `The term` WITH
    `causes a significant imbalance in rights and obligations` IS TRUE
    `the advantaged party proved it reasonably necessary to protect its legitimate interests` IS TRUE
    `would cause me detriment if applied or relied on` IS TRUE
    `defines the main subject matter of the contract` IS FALSE
    `sets the upfront price` IS FALSE
    `is required or expressly permitted by a law` IS FALSE
    `is a transparent insurance excess disclosed before the contract` IS FALSE

`the interest rate itself` MEANS `The term` WITH
    `causes a significant imbalance in rights and obligations` IS TRUE
    `the advantaged party proved it reasonably necessary to protect its legitimate interests` IS FALSE
    `would cause me detriment if applied or relied on` IS TRUE
    `defines the main subject matter of the contract` IS FALSE
    `sets the upfront price` IS TRUE
    `is required or expressly permitted by a law` IS FALSE
    `is a transparent insurance excess disclosed before the contract` IS FALSE

`Jarrah's bank account terms` MEANS `My contract` WITH
    `is a consumer contract` IS FALSE
    `is a small business contract` IS TRUE
    `is a standard form contract` IS TRUE
    `is a financial product or a contract for financial services` IS TRUE
    `is the constitution of a company` IS FALSE

`d043: Jarrah's constitution` MEANS `My contract` WITH
    `is a consumer contract` IS FALSE
    `is a small business contract` IS FALSE
    `is a standard form contract` IS TRUE
    `is a financial product or a contract for financial services` IS FALSE
    `is the constitution of a company` IS TRUE

`a negotiated loan for Jarrah` MEANS `My contract` WITH
    `is a consumer contract` IS FALSE
    `is a small business contract` IS TRUE
    `is a standard form contract` IS FALSE
    `is a financial product or a contract for financial services` IS TRUE
    `is the constitution of a company` IS FALSE

`d043: a revenue forecast to the investor with no grounds shown` MEANS `The representation` WITH
    `misleading or deceptive, or likely to mislead or deceive` IS FALSE
    `about a future matter` IS TRUE
    `evidence was adduced of reasonable grounds and they were found` IS FALSE

`d043: the same forecast, with reasonable grounds shown` MEANS `The representation` WITH
    `misleading or deceptive, or likely to mislead or deceive` IS FALSE
    `about a future matter` IS TRUE
    `evidence was adduced of reasonable grounds and they were found` IS TRUE

`Jarrah in March 2031` MEANS `The party` WITH
    `contracts in the course of carrying on a business` IS TRUE
    `persons employed, counted under s 12BF(6)` IS 0
    `turnover for its last income year` IS 0

`a firm of 150 turning over 30 million` MEANS `The party` WITH
    `contracts in the course of carrying on a business` IS TRUE
    `persons employed, counted under s 12BF(6)` IS 150
    `turnover for its last income year` IS 30000000

§ `ss 11, 12A -- ASIC's role`

-- d043: registering Jarrah is the Corporations Act's; the business name, the Business Names Registration Act's (s 12A(1)(k)).
#ASSERT `Where does ASIC's role come from` `registering or running a company` EQUALS `the corporations legislation (s 11(1)); registration is under the Corporations Act`

§ `s 12BAB -- financial services`

-- d043: issuing shares is dealing (s 12BAB(7)(b)); the own-behalf exception does not save an issuer (s 12BAB(9)).
#ASSERT `Is it a financial service` `d043: Jarrah issuing its shares to the investor`
#ASSERT `Is it a financial service` `k048: the bank supplying Jake a credit card`

§ `s 12BC -- consumer`

#ASSERT `What is the s 12BC prescribed amount` 0 EQUALS 40000

#ASSERT `Is my business a small business under s 12BC` 3 FALSE

-- k064: Jake's card is of a household kind, so the price does not matter.
#ASSERT `Did I acquire the financial services as a consumer` `k064: Jake's credit card, a household kind of service`
#ASSERT NOT (`Did I acquire the financial services as a consumer` `a 60000 business loan service, not of a business kind`)
#ASSERT `Did I acquire the financial services as a consumer` `Jarrah's 60000 business account, of a business kind`

§ `ss 12BF-12BL -- unfair terms`

-- d043: Jarrah, with no employees yet, signs on standard terms; a 5,000,001 loan is outside s 12BF(4)(a).
#ASSERT `Is it a small business contract` 200000 `Jarrah in March 2031`
#ASSERT NOT (`Is it a small business contract` 200000 `a firm of 150 turning over 30 million`)

#ASSERT NOT (`Is the term unfair` `the same term, shown reasonably necessary`)

-- d043: the company's constitution is outside Subdivision BA (s 12BL(1)); a negotiated contract is not standard form.
#ASSERT `Is the term void as unfair` `Jarrah's bank account terms` `a bank term letting it vary the fees at will`
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the term void as unfair` `Jarrah's bank account terms` `the interest rate itself`)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the term void as unfair` `d043: Jarrah's constitution` `a bank term letting it vary the fees at will`)

§ `ss 12CB, 12BB, 12DA, 12DJ -- conduct`

#ASSERT `Does the conduct contravene s 12CB` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE

#ASSERT `Is the representation misleading` `d043: a revenue forecast to the investor with no grounds shown`
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the representation misleading` `d043: the same forecast, with reasonable grounds shown`)

-- d043: the placement is exempt from disclosure (Corporations Act s 708), so no s 728 document carves the pitch out of s 12DA.
#ASSERT `Does the conduct contravene s 12DA` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the conduct contravene s 12DA` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)

-- k064: collectors of Jake's credit card debt who harass him unduly contravene s 12DJ; a firm demand does not.
#ASSERT `Does the conduct contravene s 12DJ` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the conduct contravene s 12DJ` FALSE TRUE TRUE)

§ `ss 12DL, 12DMA -- unsolicited cards and services`

-- k048: Jake applied in writing for both cards; a third card he never asked for may not be sent.
#ASSERT `May the issuer send me the card` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`May the issuer send me the card` FALSE FALSE FALSE)

#ASSERT NOT (`Must I pay for the services` FALSE TRUE)

§ `ss 12EB-12ED -- warranties`

#ASSERT NOT (`Do I have the warranty of due care and skill` TRUE TRUE TRUE)

#ASSERT NOT (`Do I have the warranty of fitness for my purpose` TRUE TRUE TRUE)

#ASSERT `Is the warranty exclusion void` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the warranty exclusion void` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)

§ `s 12GF -- damages`

-- k064: a cause of action accruing on 6 February 2037 must be sued on by 6 February 2043.
#ASSERT `By when must I sue for damages` 20370206 EQUALS 20430206

#ASSERT NOT (`Can my damages be reduced for my own carelessness` TRUE TRUE TRUE)

§ `ss 12GB-12GBCA -- penalties`

#ASSERT NOT (`Is it a civil penalty provision` `s 12DA, misleading or deceptive conduct`)

#ASSERT `Is it a s 12GB offence` `s 12DJ, harassment or coercion`

-- Penalty unit ASSUMED at 330. Daniel as an individual: 1,650,000, or three times a 1,000,000 benefit.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be ordered to pay as an individual` 330 0 EQUALS 1650000
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be ordered to pay as an individual` 330 1000000 EQUALS 3000000

-- Jarrah turning over 2 million: 50,000 units. A 10 billion turnover hits the 2.5 million unit cap.
#ASSERT `What is the most my company can be ordered to pay` 330 0 2000000 EQUALS 16500000
#ASSERT `What is the most my company can be ordered to pay` 330 0 10000000000 EQUALS 825000000

§ `Part 3 -- ASIC's examination of the founder`

-- d043 (assumed inquiry): self-incrimination is no excuse for Daniel (s 68(1)); his answers, if he claimed privilege first, are kept out of a later prosecution.
#ASSERT `Must I comply with ASIC's notice` TRUE `it might incriminate me or expose me to a penalty`
#ASSERT NOT (`Must I comply with ASIC's notice` TRUE `another reasonable excuse`)

#ASSERT NOT (`Can my examination answer be used against me` TRUE TRUE `a criminal or penalty proceeding about something else`)
#ASSERT `Can my examination answer be used against me` TRUE TRUE `a proceeding about the falsity of my statement`

